// BUG REPRO (decimal summand): the aggregation summand must be a `Long`. Here
// `sum s` adds together `s`, bound to the decimal field `input.score`. Dogwood
// arithmetic operates only on `Long` values, not decimals — matching Cedar,
// whose +, -, * operate only on Long and offer no decimal arithmetic. Summing
// decimals is also silently divergent between the two backends: the in-memory
// interpreter drops decimal rows entirely (its `sum_column` keeps only
// `as_int()` values and returns an i64), while the SQL compiler sums them as
// NUMERIC — so the same policy yields different results per engine.
//
// The summand's type was never checked, so this validated cleanly. It should
// be rejected by the temporal type-checker.
//
// Expected: rejected at `validate`.
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource)
when temporal {
    exists (n: Long). (
        (sum s for (s: decimal). where (Drupe::Action::"Charge"::request{ input.score: s })) == n
        && n > 0
    )
};
